le pieces, and is hard for Black to challenge immediately. After d2-d4, White gains a spatial advantage and improves coordination.\n\nReason:  \nP: d2-d4 is the most principled and aggressive move that maximizes central control and piece activity. It aligns with opening theory and improves White’s chances significantly by dominating the center.\n\nAnswer: P: d2-d4'}
