olidate. Similarly, playing pawns like a2-a4 or f2-f4 are less urgent.\n\nReason:  \nEn passant captures are rare and often strong when available. Here, **P: d4-e5** is both a tempo-gaining and center-controlling move that exploits Black’s recent pawn push. It is likely to give White a freer hand in development and central dominance. Delaying it forfeits the chance permanently due to the rules of en passant.\n\nAnswer: P: d4-e5'}
