ure queen exposure. Similarly, P: a2-a4 or P: h2-h4 are less impactful as they don’t contribute to center control.\n\nReason: Developing the knight to c3 is a principled opening move that supports central control, prepares castling, and avoids unnecessary pawn advances. It is consistent with opening theory and maximizes piece activity in the early game.\n\nAnswer: N: b1-c3'}
