king the f-pawn, unlike Nh3.\n\nReason: N: g1-f3 is one of the most principled opening moves. It develops a knight toward the center, increases control over key central squares (e5, d4), supports potential e4-e5 advances, and prepares kingside castling. It’s safe, flexible, and aligns with opening theory. Unlike pawn moves like a4 or h4, it contributes directly to central control and piece activity.\n\nAnswer: N: g1-f3"}
