y counterplay.\n\nReason:  \nc2-c3 is a solid developing move that supports central control and avoids weaknesses, while preparing for rapid piece development. It’s more constructive than random pawn advances and safer than pushing d5 further into danger.\n\nAnswer: P: c2-c3"}
